Package: pistomp-bluetooth
Version: 1.0.0-1~pre1
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Depends: bluez
Maintainer: pistomp <pistomp@example.com>
Description: BLE-MIDI capability for pi-Stomp
 Ships a bluetooth.service drop-in that starts bluetoothd with -E, which is
 what registers bluez's BLE-MIDI GATT profile, and unblocks the rfkill soft
 block the radio boots with. That soft block is not Pi 5 specific: a Pi 3A+
 boots with /sys/class/rfkill/rfkill0 type=bluetooth soft=1 just as a Pi 5
 does, so the drop-in is needed on every board and must not be gated on
 model. Once a BLE-MIDI device connects, bluez publishes an ALSA seq port
 and jackd -X seq bridges it automatically.
 .
 Installing this package does not turn Bluetooth on; the drop-in is inert
 while bluetooth.service is disabled. The pi-Stomp UI owns enable/disable
 and all pairing.
